\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Computational economics at $Q=500$ (analysis-grade). The oracle gap ($122.5\,\mathrm  {ms}$) is the maximum saving available to any selector. Library overhead ($472.0\,\mathrm  {ms}$) exceeds it by almost fourfold; compiled overhead ($35.5\,\mathrm  {ms}$) is affordable but the selected solvers cumulatively cost $20.0\,\mathrm  {ms}$ more than the fixed policy, so the residual limit is decision quality.}}{7}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:economics}{{4}{7}{}{figure.4}{}}
